Let a REGISTER replace the earlier bindings of the same UE (TS 24.229 5.4.1.2.1).

ims_usrloc_scscf matches a binding by its Contact URI only (contact_match()
and friends); +sip.instance and reg-id are stored with the binding's params
but nothing reads them. A UE that registers again from a new IP address or
port therefore gets a second binding, and the old one stays until it
expires: lookup() forks terminating requests to it, the 200 OK lists it,
and the P-CSCF keeps its contact and IPsec tunnel, since only a terminated
reg-event contact removes those.

usrloc now keeps the private user identity that registered each binding:
ucontact.private_identity, the new private_identity column of the contact
table (version 7, NULL for older rows) and, for a binding restored from the
HSS, the User-Name of the SCSCF-Restoration-Info AVP. save() takes it from
the username of the REGISTER's credentials only: without them
cscf_get_private_identity() falls back to the IMPU, the same string for
every UE sharing it.

Once the Contacts of a REGISTER are inserted or updated, every other valid
binding of the IMPU that one of them replaces is de-registered (always on,
there is no modparam):

- Only a binding of the same IMPI is replaced: another IMPI sharing the
  public user identity (TS 23.228 4.3.3.4) is another UE, and a binding
  whose IMPI is not known is left alone.
- A Contact with a reg-id (multiple registrations, RFC 5626) replaces the
  registration flow with the same +sip.instance (URN compared without its
  angle brackets) and reg-id - step 3.
- A Contact without one replaces every other registration of the IMPI -
  step 2 - whatever its +sip.instance, or none.
- An emergency (sos) Contact only replaces an emergency binding and a normal
  one only a normal one (5.4.1.2.1D NOTE 2). A Contact being removed
  (expires 0) replaces nothing, and a binding the REGISTER itself inserted
  or refreshed is never replaced, so several Contacts registered together
  stay.

The replaced binding is unlinked from the IMPU on the spot, after a NOTIFY to
the IMPU's subscribers that carries it as an explicit de-registration
contact, terminated with event "unregistered": 5.4.2.1.2 allows only
"unregistered", "deactivated" or "rejected" for "each replaced or removed
binding", and a P-CSCF acts only on those under an active registration
(5.2.5.2). The event type is IMS_REGISTRAR_CONTACT_UNREGISTERED_IMPLICIT:
_UNREGISTERED and _EXPIRED make create_notifications() send
Subscription-State: terminated, which would end the P-CSCF's subscription
while the IMPU is still registered over the new contact.
update_contacts_helper() runs once per IMPU of the registration, so each
IMPU unlinks and notifies its own copy; generate_reginfo_full() skips an
explicit de-registration contact that is still validly bound to the IMPU it
renders, which lists it with its own state.

process_xml_for_explit_dereg_contact() renders every explicit
de-registration contact with event "unregistered" instead of "expired": the
other producers, the de-REGISTER in save.c and reg_rpc_dereg_impu(), remove
a binding too, and "unregistered" is what RFC 3680 and 5.4.2.1.2 / 5.4.1.5
call that.

